format session-log-v1
stamp 20260819.164844
editor Claude Code
model claude-opus-5
voice Kyri
host Vultr SEA NixOS VPS ai-jail pier (Daylight DC-1 hand) -- Eastern (EDT)
title Caravan gap -- a middle falls mid-lap, and a safe restart turns out to be a silent one
prompt Keaton set the autonomous loop running: be Kyri in Radiant Style, read the card and the itineraries, close open agent-closable reds first, take the next agent-doable lap Lindy-first crux-first on the Microkernel Target double-seat, send each finished increment as its own signed round, stop at the custody gates.

think Read KYRI.md and RADIANT_STYLE.md first, so the voice shaped the round from the first token; then crux/REMEMBER.md, the top three rows of session-logs/README.md, and the newest log's recommend line -- which named the next crux exactly: the ring under fall, one domain of the circuit falling mid-lap while asks stand in the arcs on either side of it.
think Standfast on reds before new work. The living REDS rows are 80, 83, 84, 85; each carries a closure note proven on metal (the crypto count guard, the living-card ASCII guard, the crux allowlist, the witness-claim-check loom). Re-ran the two standing guards this lap -- living_card_ascii_witness and witness_claim_check_witness -- both GREEN, so no agent-closable red stood open and the constructive lane was clear.
think Council rota by lap index: 460 .kyri logs, 460 mod 27 = 1, so the deep-read was foundations/README.md -- the room that names why the front doors and foundations are the highest-leverage prose we own, and grounds Lindy-first crux-first.
think Read cycle.rye whole before writing a line beside it, plus restart.rye's fall wire and rederive.rye's per-attempt derivation, so the new rung composes rather than reinvents. Reused cycle's plan wire verbatim -- Verb, Task, read_plan, write_plan -- and carried the fall word in its own argv slot exactly as restart.rye does, so a second spelling of a plan could never drift from the first. That wanted cycle.verb_word made pub; done with a comment naming who reads it and why.
think Designed the fall points from what a pass actually consumes and produces. A pass hears a bell and writes a batch, so the two points worth dropping it at sit either side of the write. Measurement corrected an assumption here: I expected hear_from to consume the bell, and reading roundtrip.rye showed it is a read-only monotone counter -- the bell stands through a fall, which is restart.rye's own finding. So the after_hear fall proves the reassuring half rather than a loss.
think The crux fell out of the after_write case and it is the real finding of the rung. A step written to be safe to take twice finds, on its second taking, nothing left to do -- and so does nothing, including the one thing actually left undone. birch writes its onward batch, falls before ringing cedar, and the returning attempt reports nothing new and rings nobody. The bytes are whole; the lap stalls one arc short of home. Idempotence over bytes is what makes a restart safe, and it is also what makes a restart silent.
think Named the cure as a declared reading rather than baking one in, following rederive.rye's own habit with its three drift policies: wake-when-moved rings only when this attempt moved bytes, wake-every-pass rings whenever the pass completes. Both run in the self-test, so the stall is proven rather than asserted, and the difference between a ring that closes after a fall and a ring that stands still holding all its work is one line.
think Second discipline that fell out: a pass must be held to where its arc STANDS once the move is done, never to how far this attempt moved it -- a restarted step measuring its own progress reads a correct no-op as a failure. Changed the postcondition from pending == count to head == count for exactly that reason.
think Proved both RED paths on metal before trusting the green, as this arc always does. Running the mended lap under the strict reading left the returning middle reporting nothing new where the plan expected a carry, refused OutcomeMismatch, exit 1. Injecting the fall on every attempt rather than the first alone exhausted the attempt bound, refused FellTooOften, exit 1. Reverted both probes and rebuilt before claiming anything.

obs The rung landed GREEN on its first metal pass, and every claim in the witness reads the self-test output natively (assert out contains) rather than handing captured output to a shell -- REDS #76/#85, the apostrophe loom, honored by construction in a new witness rather than retrofitted.
obs A stamp red caught before it landed: I typed the round's stamp (20260819.171204) rather than reading the clock, and the live clock read 20260819.164844 -- an hour and a half in the future. Caught by running TZ=America/New_York date rather than trusting the number already on the page, and swept out of gap.rye, caravan/README.md, and the witness before any commit. This is REDS #63's own lesson recurring; it never entered the tree, so it accretes here as testimony rather than as a new ledger row. Live-clock stamps are read, never composed.
obs Narrow scope held: no new declaration, no new verb, no new outcome word. The shape under test is the ring cycle.rye already proved, and the only new vocabulary is the fall point and the wake reading -- both of which are the question the rung asks.
obs REMEMBER stayed single-stranded: the cycle edge folded into the prior-edges pointer with its finding kept in one sentence, and the gap edge seated as the live work-front with its next crux named.

loom witness=caravan_gap_witness result=GREEN rings=3 falls=2 attempts=5 derivations=5 asks_home_clean=2 asks_home_stalled=0 asks_home_mended=2 red_probes=2

file caravan/gap.rye the rung itself -- a middle falls mid-lap, the debt read off the regions rather than the process, and the wake made idempotent so the hole closes
file caravan/cycle.rye verb_word made pub with a comment naming its second reader, so one spelling of a plan word serves both supervisors
file tools/caravan_gap_witness.rish the witness, GREEN on metal, both RED paths proven before the green was trusted
file caravan/README.md the ladder row and the durable prose -- why a safe restart is also a silent one
file crux/REMEMBER.md the live edge moves to the gap, the cycle edge condensed into the prior-edges pointer

recommend keep-going -- next the ring under a fall that never returns: a middle declined by name after its bounded attempts, and what the rest of the circuit is entitled to do with a lap whose hole stays open. gap.rye already refuses FellTooOften; the open crux is whether the other domains may proceed around a permanently absent middle, or whether a ring's whole value is that they may not. No key, no funds, no gate.
